## Why Asked
Tests understanding of Kubernetes architecture and container orchestration fundamentals.

## Key Concepts
- Plugin architecture for container runtimes
- Kubelet communication layer
- Runtime-agnostic design
- Pluggable container runtime support

## Code Example
```
// CRI runtime service interface
service RuntimeService {
    // Create a new container
    CreateContainer(CreateContainerRequest) returns (CreateContainerResponse)

    // Start a container
    StartContainer(StartContainerRequest) returns (StartContainerResponse)

    // Stop a container
    StopContainer(StopContainerRequest) returns (StopContainerResponse)
}```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests cross-region coordination, CRD design, and a complex reconciliation loop under failure scenarios. It probes your ability to model ownership, promotion rules, and rollback in a production-grade system.

## Key Concepts

- Kubernetes CRD and controller design for multi-region stateful workloads
- Two-phase commit style ownership transfer and optimistic concurrency control
- Leader election, per-region reconciliation, and finalizers for safe cleanup
- Observability: conditions, events, metrics, and drift detection

